 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 511362,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Find the <span data-math=\"x\">x</span>-intercept and <span data-math=\"y\">y</span>-intercept on the given graph.\n<br>\n<figure>\n<img src=\"exercises/media/4d2ded21f121ee36.jpg\" alt=\"A line is plotted on an x y coordinate plane. The x and y axes range from negative 6 to 6, in increments of 1. The line passes through the following points, (negative 3, negative 5), (0, negative 2), (2, 0), and (6, 4).\">\n</figure>",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "The graph crosses the <span data-math=\"x\">x</span>-axis at the point (2, 0). The <span data-math=\"x\">x</span>-intercept is (2, 0). The graph crosses the <span data-math=\"y\">y</span>-axis at the point (0, −2). The <span data-math=\"y\">y</span>-intercept is (0, −2)."
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The <i>y</i>-coordinate of the point where the line crosses the <i>x</i>-axis is zero. For this line, that point is (2, 0). The point where the line crosses the <i>x</i>-axis has the form <span data-math=\"\\left( {a,0} \\right)\"></span> and is called the <i>x</i>-intercept of the line. For this line, the <i>x</i>-intercept is (2,0).</p>\n<p>In each line, the <i>x-</i>coordinate of the point where the line crosses the <i>y-</i>axis is zero. For this line, that point is (0, –2). The point where the line crosses the <i>y</i>-axis has the form <span data-math=\"\\left( {0,b} \\right)\"></span> and is called the <i>y-</i>intercept of the line. The <i>y-</i>intercept occurs where <i>x</i> is zero. For this line, the <i>y</i>-intercept is (0, –2).</p>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
